package com.cimanow

/**
 * A snapshot of cimanow's theme stylesheet, compiled into the plugin.
 *
 * ## Why this file exists
 *
 * The watch page's only external cimanow stylesheet is
 * `/wp-content/themes/Cima Now New/Assets/css/animate.css`, and this device cannot fetch it. Measured
 * 2026-08-05: `HttpURLConnection`, OkHttp, curl and — decisively — an in-page `fetch()` from a real
 * WebView on cimanow's own origin are all answered with the site's 403 block page
 * (`<title>ستوب! المخرج عايز كدة</title>`). From a clean address every one of those clients gets
 * `200 text/css`. The variable is the egress IP, not the client, so no transport, header or cookie
 * change can win it back. Serving a local copy is the only route that does not depend on the network.
 *
 * ## Why the whole file and not a CDN library
 *
 * The name is misleading. It is a concatenation, and only the bulk of it is the public animate.css
 * (83 `@keyframes`, v3-style unprefixed classes). Bundled with it are two `@font-face` rules for the
 * site's own "Cima Now" faces and ~37 theme rules — including `#watch li[aria-label="embed"] iframe`,
 * which styles the watch page's player frame. Pointing at cdnjs would restore the animations and lose
 * exactly the rules that matter here.
 *
 * ## Cost of bundling, stated plainly
 *
 * `.cs3` is a zip of `manifest.json` + `classes.dex` and carries no resources, so a stylesheet can only
 * travel as code. Hence the chunked literals: the JVM caps one string constant at 65535 bytes, and this
 * file is 72,090 bytes. The chunks are deliberately **not** `const`, so the compiler cannot fold
 * them back into one oversized constant.
 *
 * This copy goes stale when the site edits its theme. That is accepted: it is served only when the live
 * file could not be had at all, so the comparison is against an unstyled page, never against the real
 * stylesheet. Fonts and background images referenced inside it still point at cimanow and will still be
 * refused, so expect correct layout with fallback typefaces.
 *
 * ## Refreshing it
 *
 * From a network cimanow does not block, in a real browser on any cimanow page:
 * ```js
 * await (await fetch('/wp-content/themes/Cima%20Now%20New/Assets/css/animate.css?v=1.1.1.0')).text()
 * ```
 * then re-chunk the result into the literals below.
 *
 * Captured 2026-08-05 from `?v=1.1.1.0` — sha256:754d5061155e7524, 72,090 bytes.
 */
